    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 `telephone` formatted for humans (e.g. `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\nThree small, low-impact changes:\n\n1. **New util `TelephoneFormatter`** (`util/TelephoneFormatter.java`) \u2014 one static `toDisplay` method: prints `+CC`, a space, then national digits grouped in threes. It's a fresh cohesive unit with essentially no surrounding complexity to hold, and it leaves the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` untouched. Country-code length matches the two codes the app already knows (`+1` \u2192 1 digit, everything else `+61`-style \u2192 2), and non-E.164/`null` input passes through unchanged.\n\n2. **One mapping line** in `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` \u2014 a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` that delegates to the util (fully-qualified, matching the file's existing style). No method bodies grew.\n\n3. **Schema field** in `openapi.yml` \u2014 a `readOnly` `telephoneDisplay` property on the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries it.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` and all existing tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test in the acceptance suite; full run green).",
